  "toyota_summary": "Middle East instability is disrupting logistics and trade routes that automakers depend on for parts shipments and regional sales. Supply chains already stretched thin are facing new chokepoints, and companies operating in the region are reassessing inventory strategies and delivery timelines. Watch whether insurers raise premiums for shipments through the Strait of Hormuz.\n\nChina's government signaled it will accelerate spending and introduce new stimulus measures in the second half of 2026, a potential lift for demand after months of slowing sales. Automakers with heavy exposure to the Chinese market face a timing question: whether this support will be meaningful enough to reverse buyer hesitation, or merely cushion a declining trend. The details of Beijing's stimulus package arrive within weeks.",
