      "sender_norm": "POLITICO",
      "subject": "Brussels wants ‘Buy European’ but voters lean domestic",
      "pdf": "data/pdfs/20260818_1920_Brussels_wants_‘Buy_European’_but_voters_lean_dome.pdf",
      "date_label": "AUG 18  19:20",
      "read_min": 4,
      "toyota": true,
      "excerpt": "EU は公共調達で「ヨーロッパ製品優遇」政策を進めているが、大多数の加盟国の有権者は自国産",
      "subject_en": "Brussels wants ‘Buy European’ but voters lean domestic",
      "html": "data/pdfs/20260818_1920_Brussels_wants_‘Buy_European’_but_voters_lean_dome.html",
      "summary_en": "A new Public First poll shows voters in 23 of 25 EU countries favor procurement rules that prioritize domestically made goods over products from elsewhere in Europe, complicating Brussels' push for a 'Buy European' clause in its upcoming Industrial Accelerator Act. Support for national preference averages just above 50%, versus just under half for EU-wide preference, though Germany shows weak support for either and Portugal and Spain back both strongly. The findings highlight tension between the European Commission's goal of boosting EU industry through procurement and lingering nationalist economic sentiment among voters.",
      "summary_ja": "Public First社の新たな世論調査によると、EU加盟25カ国中23カ国で、有権者は欧州製品よりも自国製品を優先する公共調達ルールを支持しており、欧州委員会が進める「バイ・ヨーロピアン」条項を含む産業加速化法案の行方に影を落としている。自国優先の支持率は平均50%強で、欧州優先支持は50%弱にとどまるが、ドイツはどちらの支持も弱く、ポルトガルとスペインは両方とも強く支持するなど国によるばらつきが大きい。この結果は、EU産業振興を目指す欧州委員会の狙いと、有権者の根強い自国優先志向との間の緊張を浮き彫りにしている。",
      "summary_pdf": ""
    },
