      "ts": "20260818_0009",
      "sender_norm": "POLITICO",
      "subject": "European subsidies fuel China’s EV export boom",
      "pdf": "data/pdfs/20260818_0009_European_subsidies_fuel_China’s_EV_export_boom.pdf",
      "date_label": "AUG 18  00:09",
      "read_min": 6,
      "toyota": true,
      "excerpt": "欧州政府、特にドイツとイタリアは、中国製EV販売の急増に対応するため、電動車補助金制度の",
      "subject_en": "European subsidies fuel China’s EV export boom",
      "html": "data/pdfs/20260818_0009_European_subsidies_fuel_China’s_EV_export_boom.html",
      "summary_en": "German and Italian EV subsidies designed to spur clean-car adoption are inadvertently boosting Chinese EV sales, which jumped 65% in Europe during H1 2026 to nearly 792,000 units. Policymakers are now weighing local content requirements, following France and the UK, to prevent taxpayer funds from subsidizing Chinese competitors, though German automakers worry restrictions could trigger retaliation from Beijing given their reliance on the Chinese market.",
      "summary_ja": "ドイツやイタリアが導入したEV購入補助金が、意図せず中国製EVの販売を押し上げており、2026年上半期の欧州における中国製EV販売は前年比65%増の約79万2000台に達した。フランスや英国に続き、各国政府は税金が中国メーカーの利益になることを防ぐため、地場調達要件の導入を検討している。一方でドイツの自動車メーカーは、中国市場への依存から規制強化が北京の報復を招くことを懸念している。",
      "summary_pdf": ""
    },
